{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "quickbite-collection-v1",
    "name": "QuickBite API",
    "description": "QuickBite microservices API collection.\n\nSetup:\n1. Import this file into Postman\n2. Import QuickBite.postman_environment.json\n3. Select 'QuickBite — Local' environment from the top-right dropdown\n\nFlow:\n- Run 'Register' first to create a user\n- Run 'Login' — access_token and refresh_token are saved automatically\n- All protected requests use {{access_token}} automatically\n\nWhen new endpoints are added, re-import this file (Postman will ask to replace the existing collection).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth Service",
      "description": "Handles registration, login, JWT access tokens, and refresh tokens.\n\nBase URL: {{base_url}} (default: http://localhost:3000)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Check if the auth service and its database are up.\n\nExpected response: 200 OK\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"service\": \"auth-service\",\n  \"database\": \"up\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-08T...\"\n}\n\nError cases:\n- 503 Service Unavailable — database is unreachable"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "OTP — Request",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "    if (res.devOtp) {",
                  "        pm.environment.set('dev_otp', res.devOtp);",
                  "        console.log('devOtp saved to environment: ' + res.devOtp);",
                  "    }",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"+919876543210\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/otp/request",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "otp", "request"]
            },
            "description": "Send a 6-digit OTP to an Indian phone number (+91XXXXXXXXXX).\n\nPRIMARY auth flow. Without MSG91 credentials configured, the response includes devOtp (saved to the environment automatically) so you can test.\n\nExpected response: 200 OK\n{\n  \"message\": \"OTP sent\",\n  \"expiresInSeconds\": 300,\n  \"devOtp\": \"123456\"  // dev mode only\n}\n\nError cases:\n- 400 Bad Request — invalid phone format\n- 429 Too Many Requests — more than 3 requests per 15 minutes"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "OTP — Verify (login/register)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.environment.set('access_token', res.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('refresh_token', res.refreshToken);",
                  "    console.log('Tokens saved. isNewUser: ' + res.isNewUser);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"+919876543210\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{dev_otp}}\",\n  \"role\": \"CUSTOMER\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/otp/verify",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "otp", "verify"]
            },
            "description": "Verify the OTP. Registers the phone automatically if it's new (role applies only then; defaults to CUSTOMER).\n\n{{dev_otp}} is filled automatically by 'OTP — Request' in dev mode. With real SMS, type the received code.\n\nOn success, access_token and refresh_token are saved automatically.\n\nExpected response: 200 OK\n{\n  \"accessToken\": \"...\",\n  \"refreshToken\": \"...\",\n  \"isNewUser\": true,\n  \"user\": { \"id\": \"...\", \"phone\": \"+91...\", \"role\": \"CUSTOMER\" }\n}\n\nError cases:\n- 401 Unauthorized — invalid, expired, or already-used OTP; or too many wrong attempts"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — Customer",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"customer@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Password123!\",\n  \"role\": \"CUSTOMER\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Register a new customer account.\n\nExpected response: 201 Created\n{\n  \"id\": \"uuid\",\n  \"email\": \"customer@example.com\",\n  \"role\": \"CUSTOMER\"\n}\n\nError cases:\n- 400 Bad Request — missing or invalid fields\n- 409 Conflict — email already registered"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — Owner",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"owner@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Password123!\",\n  \"role\": \"OWNER\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Register a new restaurant owner account.\n\nExpected response: 201 Created\n{\n  \"id\": \"uuid\",\n  \"email\": \"owner@example.com\",\n  \"role\": \"OWNER\"\n}\n\nError cases:\n- 400 Bad Request — missing or invalid fields\n- 409 Conflict — email already registered"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.environment.set('access_token', res.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('refresh_token', res.refreshToken);",
                  "    console.log('access_token and refresh_token saved to environment.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('Login failed — tokens not saved.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"customer@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Password123!\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Login with email and password.\n\nOn success, the test script automatically saves access_token and refresh_token to the environment. You do not need to copy them manually.\n\nExpected response: 200 OK\n{\n  \"accessToken\": \"eyJ...\",\n  \"refreshToken\": \"eyJ...\"\n}\n\nError cases:\n- 400 Bad Request — missing fields\n- 401 Unauthorized — wrong email or password"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login — Owner",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.environment.set('access_token', res.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('refresh_token', res.refreshToken);",
                  "    console.log('access_token and refresh_token saved to environment.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('Login failed — tokens not saved.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"owner@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Password123!\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Login as an owner. Saves tokens to environment automatically."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.environment.set('access_token', res.accessToken);",
                  "    console.log('access_token refreshed and saved to environment.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('Refresh failed.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refresh_token}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Exchange the refresh token for a new access token.\n\nThe {{refresh_token}} variable is filled automatically after Login.\nOn success, access_token is updated automatically.\n\nExpected response: 200 OK\n{\n  \"accessToken\": \"eyJ...\"\n}\n\nError cases:\n- 401 Unauthorized — refresh token is invalid or expired"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refresh_token}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Revoke the refresh token. Requires a valid access token.\n\nExpected response: 200 OK\n{\n  \"message\": \"Logged out successfully\"\n}\n\nError cases:\n- 401 Unauthorized — access token missing or invalid"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Restaurant Service",
      "description": "Restaurant, category, and menu management.\n\nBase URL: {{restaurant_url}} (default: http://localhost:3001)\n\nAll write endpoints require: Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}} with OWNER role.\nLogin as owner@example.com first!",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{restaurant_url}}/health",
              "host": ["{{restaurant_url}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Check if the restaurant service and its database are up.\n\nExpected response: 200 OK\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"service\": \"restaurant-service\",\n  \"database\": \"up\"\n}"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get All Restaurants",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{restaurant_url}}/restaurants",
              "host": ["{{restaurant_url}}"],
              "path": ["restaurants"]
            },
            "description": "List all active restaurants. Public — no auth required.\n\nExpected response: 200 OK — array of restaurants"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Restaurant by ID",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{restaurant_url}}/restaurants/:id",
              "host": ["{{restaurant_url}}"],
              "path": ["restaurants", ":id"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{restaurant_id}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Get a single restaurant with categories and available menu items. Public — no auth required.\n\nExpected response: 200 OK\nError cases:\n- 404 Not Found — restaurant does not exist"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create Restaurant",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('restaurant_id', pm.response.json().id);",
                  "    console.log('restaurant_id saved to environment.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Spice Garden\",\n  \"description\": \"Authentic Indian cuisine\",\n  \"address\": \"123 Main Street, Kochi\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{restaurant_url}}/restaurants",
              "host": ["{{restaurant_url}}"],
              "path": ["restaurants"]
            },
            "description": "Create a new restaurant. OWNER role required.\n\nOn success, restaurant_id is saved to the environment automatically.\n\nExpected response: 201 Created\nError cases:\n- 401 Unauthorized — missing/invalid token\n- 403 Forbidden — CUSTOMER role cannot create restaurants"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Restaurant",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"description\": \"Authentic Indian cuisine — now with tandoor specials\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{restaurant_url}}/restaurants/:id",
              "host": ["{{restaurant_url}}"],
              "path": ["restaurants", ":id"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{restaurant_id}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Update restaurant fields (name, description, address, imageUrl, isActive). Owner of this restaurant only.\n\nError cases:\n- 403 Forbidden — you do not own this restaurant\n- 404 Not Found"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Add Category",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('category_id', pm.response.json().id);",
                  "    console.log('category_id saved to environment.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Main Course\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{restaurant_url}}/restaurants/:id/categories",
              "host": ["{{restaurant_url}}"],
              "path": ["restaurants", ":id", "categories"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{restaurant_id}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Add a menu category to your restaurant. Owner only.\n\nOn success, category_id is saved to the environment automatically."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Add Menu Item",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('menu_item_id', pm.response.json().id);",
                  "    console.log('menu_item_id saved to environment.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Butter Chicken\",\n  \"description\": \"Creamy tomato-based curry\",\n  \"price\": 250.00,\n  \"categoryId\": \"{{category_id}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{restaurant_url}}/restaurants/:id/menu-items",
              "host": ["{{restaurant_url}}"],
              "path": ["restaurants", ":id", "menu-items"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{restaurant_id}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Add a menu item to your restaurant. Owner only. categoryId is optional.\n\nOn success, menu_item_id is saved to the environment automatically."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Menu Item",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"price\": 275.50,\n  \"isAvailable\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{restaurant_url}}/restaurants/:id/menu-items/:itemId",
              "host": ["{{restaurant_url}}"],
              "path": ["restaurants", ":id", "menu-items", ":itemId"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{restaurant_id}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "itemId",
                  "value": "{{menu_item_id}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Update a menu item (name, description, price, categoryId, imageUrl, isAvailable). Owner only."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete Menu Item",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{restaurant_url}}/restaurants/:id/menu-items/:itemId",
              "host": ["{{restaurant_url}}"],
              "path": ["restaurants", ":id", "menu-items", ":itemId"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{restaurant_id}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "itemId",
                  "value": "{{menu_item_id}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Remove a menu item from your restaurant. Owner only.\n\nExpected response: 204 No Content"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Order Service",
      "description": "Coming in Sprint 3.\n\nBase URL: {{order_url}} (default: http://localhost:3002)\n\nAll endpoints require: Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Place Order",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"restaurantId\": \"{{restaurant_id}}\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"menuItemId\": \"{{menu_item_id}}\",\n      \"quantity\": 2\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{order_url}}/orders",
              "host": ["{{order_url}}"],
              "path": ["orders"]
            },
            "description": "Place a new order. CUSTOMER role required.\n\n[Sprint 3]"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get My Orders",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{order_url}}/orders",
              "host": ["{{order_url}}"],
              "path": ["orders"]
            },
            "description": "Get all orders belonging to the logged-in user.\n\n[Sprint 3]"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Accept Order",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{order_url}}/orders/:id/accept",
              "host": ["{{order_url}}"],
              "path": ["orders", ":id", "accept"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{order_id}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Accept an incoming order. OWNER role required.\n\n[Sprint 3]"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Reject Order",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{order_url}}/orders/:id/reject",
              "host": ["{{order_url}}"],
              "path": ["orders", ":id", "reject"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{order_id}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Reject an incoming order. OWNER role required.\n\n[Sprint 3]"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": []
}
